{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Give [F]thanks to the Lord to[C/E]day
[Dm7]For he is good and [Am7]stays
His [Bb]mercy endures forev[F/A]er
[Gm7]Let the redeemed say so [C7sus4]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Mercy endures forev[C/E]er
[Dm7]Goodness is his [Am7]name
Praise the [Bb]Lord for his [F/A]kind[Dm7]ness
[Gm7]We are [C7sus4]not the [F]same
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C7sus4][F]He redeemed from the ene[C/E]my
Gath[Dm7]ered out of the [Am7]lands
[Bb]From east and from the [F/A]west
From north and the [Gm7]seas [C7sus4]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Some [Bb]wandered in the [Fmaj7/A]wilderness
[Gm7]A wasteland with no [F]road
[Bb]Found no city to [F/A]live in
[Dm7]Lost in the [Gm7][C7sus4]cold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Mercy endures forev[C/E]er
[Dm7]Goodness is his [Am7]name
Praise the [Bb]Lord for his [Am7]kind[Dm7]ness
[Gm7]We are [C7sus4]not the [F]same
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
His mercy endures for[C/E]ever
{end_of_verse}

